posts.body:
@Sakurra
I am sure there must be a better way to do this, but here is a way that works. You just have to set the bar either to the right edge of the screen or you could also put another picture with a higher value Picture ID where the bar picture can move under it to disappear.
Here is a screenshot of a quick, not pretty example. Essentially, you are changing the X coordinate of the bar image and moving it off the screen (or under another image). When you gain health, you change the X coordinate to move the bar back onto the screen.
So in this example, the bar image is never actually changing size. You could actually do the same thing on the other size of the screen because you can move images completely off the screen by going below 0 for X or above 816.
Again, there is probably a better way to do this, but this works.
$gameScreen.showPicture(1, 'Preview Button Blank', 0, $gameVariables.value(761), 20, 150, 100, 255, 0);

Here is an example from the MZ Script Call List.
// Turn picture 1 to 45° clockwise from its original state
$gameScreen.picture(1)._angle = 45;
I have used this to turn the picture. Pretty much pick any angle you want.
